        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten recovery-small test_50",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten recovery-small test_50\n\nrecovery-small test_50 slept 60 seconds after each MDS failover,\nand $TIMEOUT seconds at the end, to let the client reconnect.\nfail() already waits for the client imports to be ready, so\nmost of that time was idle.\n\nKeep 10 seconds of writemany load between failovers and before\nthe writer is stopped. Each failover still happens under load\nand the writer must still exit cleanly.\n\nMeasured on a single-node rocky9 VM (1 MDT, 3 OSTs), three runs\neach with ONLY=50: 216, 214 and 215 seconds before, 98, 103 and\n103 seconds after. Rainshadow shows 5399 runs in 30 days, so\nsaving about 113 seconds per run is about 170 hours per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=recovery-small env=ONLY=50\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I5d978aa16288e7ff8b08fc857a96f31b967f6f40\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70258\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
